    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d240">

                <pb facs="0434" n="302" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv01/pg302"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Potsdam/7–1145: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 240<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the
                        Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-11">July 11, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>16. Recommendation that we request British concurrence in our intention, if and
                    when Italy declares war against Japan, to support officially and publicly
                    Italy’s admission in due course to world security organization is now before the
                    President in papers prepared for Big Three meeting (See Italy: Topics on Which
                    Discussion is Desired; III, Participation in World Organizations<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d240-f1"/>). Inasmuch as it now appears that Italy may declare war
                    before Big Three meeting, and since effective value of American action both in
                    US and abroad may depend to great extent upon prompt announcement thereof
                    following Italian declaration, it is believed that we should proceed immediately
                    with recommendation.</p>
                <pb facs="0435" n="303" xml:id="pg303"/>
                <p>If you agree, and President approves, instructions will be sent Winant to inform
                    British Government and inquire if it is prepared to support American
                    position.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>[<hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
